WEBVTT

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.600
A typical commute became a scene out of a nightmare today...

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.900
...when a burning car plunged off a bridge after a high-speed chase and gun battle.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.310
Daniel Morgan is on the scene.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.490
As you can see, after it plunged off the drawbridge...

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:29.030
...into the canal, the vehicle released a huge plume of smoke.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.620
Although rescue crews were able to retrieve the car with a crane...

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.780
...no bodies have been recovered so far.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.620
George Black, director of the ATF division in charge of the investigation...

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.170
...told us that the bodies may have been swept downstream by the river.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:47.920
With the help of some civilians, we were able to break up a gun-smuggling ring.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.550
However, I would like to point out that this incident...

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:55.310
...demonstrates why "vigilantes vs. criminals" only works in the movies.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.890
We have not yet learned the names of the civilians who were involved.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.940
Indeed, who would guess that the "civilians" were getting lectured by the police?

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:08.240
The moment I get back from my first vacation in forever, this happens.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.610
You've put me in a tough spot, Rally.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.780
Don't you think you've gone a bit too far this time?

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:18.040
Aw... Kate, you're blowing this way out of proportion.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:21.120
She's not exaggerating. Just take a look outside.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:26.500
We've had to send out extra patrols on a weekend.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.090
It wasn't really our fault.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.970
That's right, Roy. We're not the ones who caused this; we're the victims.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.180
So why did you ditch the ATF agents assigned to protect you?

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:39.270
That ATF agent, Collins...

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:43.480
...told me that you refused to cooperate and made it impossible for them to protect you.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:44.650
That asshole...

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.690
Give me the file.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:46.690
Here...

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.940
We received this information from the ATF.

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:52.150
She appears to have entered the US from Canada about three days ago.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.870
That's her, all right!
Roy, who is she?

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:00.250
Natasha Radinov, ex-GRU.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.500
Currently a freelance "businesswoman."

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.330
She's also known by the code name "Bloody Pierce."

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:08.800
It seems she was doing freelance hits even back when she was in the special forces.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.420
She's a killing machine, trained in every conceivable lethal skill.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:15.050
She's basically the Terminator.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:18.390
And now she's after you, Rally.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.640
You think she's still alive...?

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:23.390
Why don't you let us worry about Radinov?

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:26.860
Your job is to take this bag and go home quietly.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.110
Wha...?
Huh? What's that?

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:31.570
It's from me and my wife...

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:33.700
I'll walk you, our heroes, out the back door.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.280
Rally, please don't go overboard again.

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:39.740
Yeah, I know.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:41.000
See you.

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.750
So much for our chance
to make some money.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:47.960
We just went through hell for nothing.

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:00.890
OK. This is her way of sending us a challenge.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:42.120
Hello, Gunsmith Cats.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:45.450
What do you mean? Yes... yes...

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.450
What on Earth is this?

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.870
Does he think we're a bunch of Japanese tourists?

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:51.000
Calm down. He meant well... Huh?

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:54.090
Hey, who was that?

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.000
State senator Heinz's secretary.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:05:00.340
It seems he wants to give us an award during his campaign rally tomorrow.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:04.510
Huh...? Senator Heinz? You mean the
guy who's been running for mayor?

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:08.390
I bet he'll throw a huge party in our honor.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:11.190
Wow, whatever shall I do if some big talent scout spots me?!

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.890
Get real... Oh...

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:14.770
Now, what were you saying?

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.440
He was very pushy.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:22.280
They want to promote his gun control program
now that the smuggling case is closed.

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:26.620
The smuggling case is closed? Don't they know Radinov is still alive?

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:29.620
We still haven't figured out who's pulling the ATF's strings.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:31.620
This might be our chance to speak to the senator directly.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:35.090
Sorry, but I'm going to have to decline.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:37.550
It'd be bad for business if everyone knew what I looked like.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.630
What? But that's such a waste...

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:42.260
I'll leave all the talent scouts to you, Minnie.

00:05:42.470 --> 00:05:47.560
But Rally, don't let your guard down for an instant. She could attack at any time.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:53.520
Hah! When she does, I'll ask her to pay for the repairs on my Cobra.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:34.390
No... this isn't good enough either...

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:37.190
Hey, Rally, which one do you think looks better on me?

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:40.530
Ah... Either one, I suppose.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.490
Hey, can you at least look?!

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:46.700
It really doesn't matter what you wear.

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:50.120
Instead, you should worry about your own safety.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:55.170
Don't you worry about me. By the way,
Rally... try those heels.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:56.420
Huh...?

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.280
I bought them for you.

00:06:58.290 --> 00:06:59.880
Those are for me?

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:03.050
Uh... Eyah!

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:04.840
See? They look great on you.

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:08.800
That's not the point... Whoa...

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:12.270
There's no way I can run in shoes like these!

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:15.100
Maybe not, but they'll make the guys run to <i>you.</i>

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:17.230
Oh sure, right.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:19.470
See? They're here!

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:21.120
Don't be silly!

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:26.110
Rally, you can take them off now.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:27.910
Oh, yeah...

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:29.320
Who's there?

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:31.410
Who're you?!

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.460
Rally, it's me, Bill! I've gotta talk to you.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:37.830
Not you again...

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:40.090
See, they attracted a man!

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:40.790
May!

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:42.840
Hee... just kidding!

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:43.960
Sheesh!

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:45.970
Come on, Rally, open up!

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.840
Hey, we have nothing to say to you!

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:55.140
As things stand, the investigation will be shut down. Please! I need your help.

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:58.730
Sorry, we found a better way to solve our problem.

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:01.480
We're going to cut a deal with a certain VIP tomorrow.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:04.400
VIP? Who do you mean?

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:06.360
None of your business!

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:08.740
I've got to get up early tomorrow, so feel free to slither away.

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:10.700
But Rally...

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:14.410
Excuse me, sir, but could you explain why you are here?

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:21.590
Look, I'm Bill Collins of the ATF. I need their help with an investigation.

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:24.380
No need to show me your ID.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:28.340
My orders are to not to let anyone approach this house, not even the president.

00:08:30.430 --> 00:08:35.020
OK, I give up! If you see the president, give him my regards.

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:42.400
He may be a man, but not the kind I want.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:07.590
Bill!

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:08.090
Hmm...?

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:09.380
Where on Earth have you been?

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.840
You're never here when something important happens.

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:16.770
Cathy, I'd give you a hug and a kiss but my hands are full.

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:19.480
We don't have time for silly jokes.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:19.480
Huh...?

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:20.640
Look at this!

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:25.360
I checked the phone records like you asked, and look what I found!

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:27.480
Uh... Huh...?

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:28.780
Number 6?

00:09:28.990 --> 00:09:32.410
Yes. That's a safe house that was supposedly shut down.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:35.080
So who's still using it?

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:38.540
George Black? No way!

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:42.500
So our boss is the mastermind behind this? Where is he?

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:46.590
He suddenly turned in a vacation request and left.

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:50.050
Don't worry, Cathy. I'll take care of this...

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:53.470
Very well done! You hit the bull's-eye.

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:54.760
Bill...

00:09:54.970 --> 00:10:00.100
But... promise me you won't tell anybody else yet. OK?

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:00.100
OK...

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.350
Good girl!

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:04.770
We'll catch dinner together sometime.
Love ya, honey.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:07.360
Oh... Bill! Oooh...

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:24.420
Radinov? Radinov! You're here, aren't you?

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:29.380
Radinov, you're OK. That's great, uh...
I was really getting worried.

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:32.340
Why, the director of the ATF is here.

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:35.800
Look, I can't keep fooling them much longer.

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:38.640
Radinov, I'm begging you.
Take me with you.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:41.850
Hmph! So you think the world revolves around you?

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:46.810
Er... I've got money. Name your price and I'll pay it.

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:50.110
Hmm... So... what should I do?

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.570
Is... Is there somebody else here?

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:58.110
Yes, I suppose we will
have to get rid of him.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:02.160
No, wait! I won't say anything!

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.830
Radinov, please tell him!

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:08.130
Did you hear that? Right.

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:14.880
P... Please...

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:17.380
Help me...

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:18.330
Radinov...

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:57.840
What the hell?! It's the chief!

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:00.000
<i>Geordi, wait.</i>

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:03.560
What's that doing there?

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:08.850
A simple booby trap. But we're
up against an expert.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:11.730
We can't be too careful.

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:19.740
Wha...? Geordi!

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:23.410
I pushed the redial. Maybe we'll find out who the last person he talked to was.

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:27.660
Didn't you hear me? We're dealing with a pro.
Don't touch anything until it's been checked.

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:31.040
Don't worry. Nothing happened.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:33.290
Oh, it's connecting.

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:36.590
"You have reached Eddie Heinz's office. Our office..."

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:38.300
Who's Eddie Heinz...?

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:41.300
A state senator and a friend of the chief's.

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:44.100
And if the chief called him from here...

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:48.020
...then Radinov, the chief, and
Heinz were working together.

00:12:50.940 --> 00:12:54.020
Rally said she was going to meet some VIP... Damn!

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:56.900
Geordi, don't touch anything else! Got that?

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:59.000
Hey, wait! Bill!

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:01.370
What's the big hurry?

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:12.630
I knew it... A pro... Rally...

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:36.650
OK. That's where we want it.

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:50.500
Just as Black said, I had better not overstay my welcome.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:54.000
However, I have one thing
I need to attend to first.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:57.090
You mean those two little girls?

00:13:57.090 --> 00:13:59.710
How about we eliminate them for you?

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:02.340
That is not necessary. This one I will do for free.

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:05.680
So it's gotten personal, has it?

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:09.640
Nyet. This is a matter of pride.

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:15.600
We've received a request for a
TV interview this afternoon.

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:22.390
Please decline. I would prefer to remain
silent until we tie up all the loose ends.

00:14:22.490 --> 00:14:23.570
Right.

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:26.780
Thank you all so much for coming out today despite the rain.

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:29.370
We will open the venue in three hours.

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:31.250
We're sorry to keep you waiting in this cold weather...

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:34.080
I don't get it.

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:37.250
They told us to be here at the crack of dawn and stay put until evening.

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:38.500
I'm so cold...

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:41.800
This is what you should expect from politicians, Rally.

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:43.760
We could leave if you'd prefer.

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:50.220
We can't do that. We need that license to reopen the shop.

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:53.430
Aw man, these pumps are all muddy.

00:14:53.770 --> 00:14:55.520
Brrrrr! It's freezing.

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:58.150
This is far from what I dreamed about...

00:14:58.360 --> 00:14:59.980
Excuse me...

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:03.780
I'm sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:06.740
Uh... Hey! What are you doing?

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:11.200
It's not that we don't trust you, but we have to protect the senator's image.

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:15.210
I'll do it myself!

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:21.300
That's quite a selection. I'm afraid we'll have to hold onto all of these for you.

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:23.050
I'll take care of them, if you don't mind.

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:24.630
And who might you be?

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:26.630
And who might you be?
Roy Coleman, City Police.

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:28.550
Do you have a problem with that?

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:31.890
Hmm... I suppose not. I'll see you later.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:34.600
What a jerk!

00:15:34.810 --> 00:15:38.940
If Heinz hires thugs like that, I don't think
I'm looking forward to meeting him.

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:40.060
Indeed...

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:48.490
Thank you for waiting! And now, may I present Edward Heinz!

00:15:48.700 --> 00:15:55.000
Eddie! Eddie...!

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:01.920
Thank you.

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:05.630
And now, without further ado, I'd like to introduce my very special guests!

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:11.390
Yes, these are the brave young women who foiled a band of ruthless gunrunners!

00:16:11.390 --> 00:16:15.850
Rally Vincent and May Hopkins!

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:19.850
Heh heh! What's the matter, ladies?
Feeling a little nervous?

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:24.360
I have a special award to present to these lovely heroes!

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:27.990
This plaque is a symbol of our appreciation...

00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:30.700
...as we, the people, commemorate their bravery and courage.

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:35.410
Rally, May, please step forward.
Don't worry, I won't bite.

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:39.790
Hey, Michael, hold the mic.

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:49.260
Rally, run!

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:06.570
That's her! May, let's go!

00:17:06.780 --> 00:17:08.610
R... Rally!

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:13.530
What's going on?! Hey, what's wrong?

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:17.130
Oh! He's the ATF agent who was in charge of the gunrunning case!

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:17.130
What?

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:19.830
It... It's a trap.

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:22.040
We've got to stop Rally and May.

00:17:22.710 --> 00:17:24.750
Don't worry. I'm with the Chicago Police.

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:25.290
Ah!

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:27.870
Roy! I got my guns back!

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:29.590
Wait! Rally!

00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:33.300
<i>That was too close. It's time</i> <i>to take the fight to her.</i>

00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:48.730
Well?

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:53.500
Yeah, it's working. May, you enter from the back. I'll go in through the front.

00:17:54.350 --> 00:17:54.870
Ready?

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:55.410
OK!

00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:58.120
Let's go!

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:58.120
Right!

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:09.010
There you are.

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:34.870
Hold it!

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:39.270
Let me warn you,
 that bulletproof coat is useless this time.

00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:41.290
One false move, and you'll be missing a head.

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:45.310
Get your hands up!

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:52.130
Now turn around. Slowly.

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:58.300
I said turn around slowly!
I've got the drop on you!

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:00.640
You won't shoot me in the back.

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:03.640
You lose!

00:19:11.570 --> 00:19:13.110
No! Rally!

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:18.280
May!

00:19:19.990 --> 00:19:21.040
May!

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:25.350
May!

00:19:36.010 --> 00:19:38.720
We meet at last, Rally Vincent.

00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:49.690
I will make you pay dearly for this little nick.

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:55.610
I want you to endure the same... no, far more pain than this.

00:19:56.860 --> 00:20:02.080
I won't let you die easily. You'll know true agony before you go.

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:07.100
Rally...

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:13.020
Run...

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:19.030
Wha...?

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:25.100
Shit...

00:20:35.650 --> 00:20:36.550
Downstairs...

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:47.370
And... cue...

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:53.420
Yes, I'm standing in front of Grant Park, where just a few moments ago...

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:56.760
...a gunman opened fire on mayoral candidate Edward Heinz.

00:20:56.960 --> 00:21:00.640
The suspect is holed up inside the museum, which is currently closed for renovations.

00:21:07.020 --> 00:21:08.730
Rally... hold on!

00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:11.560
I'm doing all right. How about you, May?

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:16.230
Heh, I'm doing just fine. I just wish I could use my hands.

00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:20.070
It's a good thing I prepped some traps in advance.

00:21:27.330 --> 00:21:28.580
Hm...?

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:55.990
Got her...

00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:01.840
What? What the hell?

00:23:03.510 --> 00:23:06.800
Hey, that's enough! Gray, I'm leaving.

00:23:06.800 --> 00:23:07.930
Er...

00:23:08.140 --> 00:23:12.890
Fortunately, the media is concentrating on Radinov right now, but...

00:23:13.100 --> 00:23:15.520
What do you mean, "fortunately"?

00:23:15.730 --> 00:23:18.940
Listen! That crazy Russian psychopath was shooting at <i>me</i> as well!

00:23:18.940 --> 00:23:20.900
I want her out of the picture! Huh?

00:23:21.860 --> 00:23:26.030
Radinov? What the hell are you doing here?

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:30.990
And what was the big idea of pointing a gun
at me while I was on the stage?!

00:23:30.990 --> 00:23:35.160
We're done doing business. And
I'd better get my heroin back.

00:23:36.620 --> 00:23:40.630
Uh, uh, calm down, Radinov...
I didn't mean that.

00:23:40.630 --> 00:23:43.840
Heh... You understand, right?

00:23:44.420 --> 00:23:47.720
That's right! We have to stick together, you know.

00:23:56.980 --> 00:24:01.020
I don't believe it! The gun control candidate... with a gun in his hand!

00:24:02.070 --> 00:24:06.360
Stricter gun laws mean higher prices for your illegal weapons, right?

00:24:06.570 --> 00:24:08.530
Did you get it?

00:24:08.030 --> 00:24:08.530
Perfectly.

00:24:10.030 --> 00:24:13.040
W... W... What the hell are you doing? Cut that camera off!

00:24:13.240 --> 00:24:14.910
Holy shit!

00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:16.620
This is huge! Let's go!

00:24:17.830 --> 00:24:18.790
Move!

00:24:21.460 --> 00:24:24.260
Senator Heinz, you're under arrest.

00:24:27.880 --> 00:24:32.220
I was so close... I could have cleaned out all the gangs and immigrants.

00:24:32.810 --> 00:24:35.850
I only did it for the good of the American people!

00:24:35.850 --> 00:24:40.690
What the heck?! Hey, get the camera, get the camera! Get a picture of Heinz's face!

00:24:41.230 --> 00:24:42.690
Call the news director!

00:24:49.160 --> 00:24:51.200
What a bunch of vultures!

00:24:51.410 --> 00:24:53.830
That's just the way reporters are, I guess.

00:24:54.620 --> 00:24:56.790
If we want to make it in this town...

00:24:56.790 --> 00:24:58.790
...we'll have to make some adjustments.

00:24:59.370 --> 00:25:03.920
Well... we're not really very flexible.

00:25:04.130 --> 00:25:06.760
Please don't remind me, May.

00:25:08.720 --> 00:25:09.680
Ready?

00:25:19.020 --> 00:25:22.190
I guess somebody else wasn't good at adjusting to reality either.

00:25:26.940 --> 00:25:28.530
Die!

00:25:32.700 --> 00:25:34.700
<i>I can't move my arm!</i>

00:25:57.600 --> 00:26:03.650
Admit it, sometimes I'm useful.
I'm a real Eliot Ness.

00:26:04.230 --> 00:26:05.980
Kinda-sorta...

00:26:07.570 --> 00:26:08.350
Are you all right?

00:26:08.360 --> 00:26:09.880
I'm OK.

00:26:10.490 --> 00:26:13.010
I can get up by myself.

00:26:21.120 --> 00:26:23.500
I have to be able to stand on my own...

00:26:34.260 --> 00:26:37.350
That's what it takes to make it in this town...
